     "t": "p",
     "text": "On **Slide 227**, the instructor introduces the foundational step-multiplication identities that govern the Unilateral Z-Transform. The mathematical behavior of unit step products in discrete time differs profoundly from continuous time due to the non-zero measure of the discrete point $n = 0$."
